@title Reading Your Quarterly Water Bill
@subtitle Tarn Valley Water, a guide for customers

# Your bill at a glance
kpi Bills are issued | Every 3 months
kpi Payment due | 21 days | after the issue date
kpi Service charge | $38.40 | per quarter

Your bill has three parts: usage charges for the water you used, a sewer charge, and a fixed service charge. Usage is metered in cubic meters (m3). Add the three parts together and you have your total.

# Usage charges
Usage is charged in three tiers, so the rate depends on how much you used:

- The first 30 m3 cost $1.85 per m3.
- The next 30 m3 cost $2.60 per m3.
- Anything above 60 m3 costs $3.90 per m3.

# Fixed charges
The sewer charge is 80 percent of your usage charge. The fixed service charge is $38.40 each quarter, whatever you use.

Here is an example for a household that used 72 m3 in a quarter:

table = Item,How it is worked out,Amount; Usage first 30 m3,30 at $1.85,$55.50; Usage next 30 m3,30 at $2.60,$78.00; Usage above 60 m3,12 at $3.90,$46.80; Usage total,55.50 + 78.00 + 46.80,$180.30; Sewer charge,80 percent of $180.30,$144.24; Service charge,fixed each quarter,$38.40; Total,180.30 + 144.24 + 38.40,$362.94

So this household's total is $362.94.

# Ways to pay
Your bill is due 21 days after the issue date. You can pay:

- Online at tarnvalleywater.example/pay
- By phone on 555-0121
- In person at the Main Street office on weekdays from 8:30 to 16:30

Autopay takes $2 off each bill.

# If you cannot pay on time
If you cannot pay by the due date, please call 555-0133 before then. We can set up a payment plan with you. A late fee of 5 percent is added after 30 days, so it is much better to call early than to wait.
